<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 66,790 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 66,790 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 66,790 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 110,535 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	June 1</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 4,822	17,731</p>
<p>    Import cargo		61,968	92,804</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and one berthed. In the next 24 hours, three are expected to sail and six are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Sulpher		 2,000	 Nova -1		    2/6</p>
<p>Containers		400	 Putney Bridge	    3/6</p>
<p>Containers		200	 Orient Star		3/6</p>
<p>Vehicles		  100	 Hual Margarits	   5/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
